{
  "_comment": "Settings template - OpenRouter (model marketplace, OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Copy this file WITHOUT the .example suffix (-> appsettings.openrouter.local.json), then set your key in the environment: ApiKeyEnvVar names the variable that holds it (OPENROUTER_API_KEY), which every run reads — a terminal, a scheduled team, the REPL — and the key itself never goes in the file (ORKEON_Llm__ApiKey, when set, wins). Identifiers are vendor/model and the vendor prefix is mandatory; suffixes :free / :nitro (throughput) / :floor (price) travel in the identifier. openrouter/auto is usable but drifts (the served model changes without notice) - the response's served_model metadata says who answered. The factory auto-detects OpenRouterLlmProvider from the openrouter.ai host. Cheap text-only alternative: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash. Not campaigned yet (LLM-09, 2026-09-18).",
  "_models": [
    "google/gemini-3.7-flash - the fleet's Gemini default under its marketplace id; ctx 1,048,576, 0.75 / 3.75 $/M in/out, text+image+video+file+audio, reasoning + response_format (json_schema) + tools (public catalog GET /api/v1/models, 2026-09-18)",
    "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash - reasoning model, cheap text-only alternative for the transport comparison (M7/M8)",
    "openai/gpt-5.6-sol - no temperature in supported_parameters: the per-model constraint (only 1) travels through the aggregator",
    "openrouter/auto - router alias, price -1 (variable): refused as a default, fine by explicit configuration",
    "Source: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models (public, no key) - 445 entries on 2026-09-18"
  ],
  "Llm": {
    "BaseUrl": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
    "Model": "google/gemini-3.7-flash",
    "ApiKeyEnvVar": "OPENROUTER_API_KEY",
    "Temperature": 0.2,
    "TimeoutSeconds": 600
  },
  "RateLimiting": {
    "MaxConcurrentRequests": 16,
    "GlobalRequestsPerMinute": 300,
    "ProviderRequestsPerMinute": 300,
    "AgentRequestsPerMinute": 10,
    "QueueLimit": 512
  },
  "LlmLogging": {
    "FullEmbeddingLog": false
  }
}
